<article class="env-remark" id="019B">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/019B">Remark <span data-tag="019B">11.8.0.5</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{Kan}}$ denote the homotopy category of Kan complexes (Construction <a data-tag="00TY" href="/tag/00TY">3.1.5.10</a>). Then $\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{Kan}}$ can be identified with the homotopy category of the $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{S}}$ of Construction <a class="" data-content="This is a reference to something which is not yet available in Kerodon." data-html="true" data-placement="bottom" data-toggle="popover" data-trigger="focus" role="button" style="cursor: pointer;" tabindex="0" title="Future reference"><img src="/static/images/question.svg"/></a>. If $q: X \rightarrow S$ is a left fibration of simplicial sets, then Construction <a data-tag="019U" href="/tag/019U">5.2.5.2</a> determines a covariant transport functor </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  T: \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{S} \rightarrow \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{Kan}}. \]
</div>
<p> In §<a class="" data-content="This is a reference to something which is not yet available in Kerodon." data-html="true" data-placement="bottom" data-toggle="popover" data-trigger="focus" role="button" style="cursor: pointer;" tabindex="0" title="Future reference"><img src="/static/images/question.svg"/></a>, we show that (up to equivalence) $T$ can be promoted to a map of simplicial sets $S \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{S}}$. In other words, the formation of covariant transport morphisms $(e: s \rightarrow s') \mapsto (e_{!}: X_{s} \rightarrow X_{s'})$ is compatible with composition not only up to homotopy, but up to <em>coherent</em> homotopy. </p>
</article>
